.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD_SECURITY 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd_security
.Nd ocifbsd security policy and resource-limit library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ocifbsd/security/rctl.h
.In ocifbsd/security/mac.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library implements the security policy and resource-limit
primitives used by
.Xr ocifbsd 8
to constrain and label containers and jails.
It is not a standalone program; it is linked into
the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary and any external tooling that needs to
manage RCTL rules, MAC labels, or seccomp-equivalent
sandboxing on FreeBSD jails.
.Pp
The library provides three functional areas:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Resource limits
.Pq rctl.c
drives the
.Xr rctl 8
command to apply, query, and remove per-jail resource
caps (memoryuse, openfiles, nproc, cputime, etc.)
and translates the OCI
.Sy Linux.resources
JSON block into the equivalent FreeBSD RCTL rules.
.It
MAC framework
.Pq mac.c
manages the
.Xr mac 4
labels that ocifbsd applies to jails, including
Biba integrity labels, MLS sensitivity labels,
and partition visibility labels. It can list,
load, and unload MAC policy modules and parse
the
.Sq Cm jail -j Ar jail Cm label= Ns ...
syntax.
.It
Seccomp shims
.Pq mac.c,
.Fn seccomp_load_profile ,
.Fn seccomp_create_jail_filter ,
.Fn seccomp_remove_filter ,
.Fn seccomp_get_syscall_list
.Pq currently stubs.
The real implementation will translate OCI seccomp
profiles into
.Xr capsicum 4
capability rights; see
.Pa /usr/local/share/doc/ocifbsd/MIGRATION.md
in the source tree for the full translation plan.
.El
.Pp
The public API is declared across
.In ocifbsd/security/rctl.h
and
.In ocifbsd/security/mac.h ;
see those headers for the full list of functions and
data structures.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/ocifbsd/security.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/security.conf
Security defaults (default MAC policy, default RCTL action).
.It Pa /var/run/ocifbsd/rctl/
Per-jail RCTL rule snapshots (human-readable,
the format produced by
.Xr rctl 8
.Fl j Ar jail ) .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8 ,
.Xr rctl 8 ,
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr biba 4 ,
.Xr mls 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
library first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
library was developed by
.An REVYTECH, Inc.
